  "question": "Does initial fork housing within/outside primary reach plus both real responses establish meaningful new player decision?",
  "conclusion": "Not by itself. Housing is damage-closed at the fork; a changed distance there does not prove a different useful recovery approach. Root should evaluate already planned actual native geometry/proof/action receipts. No new engine case or test gate is proposed.",
  "current_promoted_fixture_sha256": "94d82eab1f06949545aeaeb34da045fe320cdce4bbaad059ca4fa684668866d4",
  "hypothesis": "If native context admits the first ordered old neutral escape, the old safe no-return stationary opening becomes unsafe under the changed ray origin. The new source therefore requires a different useful escape/landing or later positioning response in this representative component. This changes an existing landing/approach choice; it need not be harder.",
  "why_range_predicate_is_weak": [
    "Original damage_window_open requires running recovery and actual locked adapter/current native presentation. Initial fork in-range is not an attack opportunity.",
    "Scheduler _prove enumerates view-filtered escape directions and zero return first, then finite authored return directions. Different source coordinates can yield either different or identical useful paths; selected proof order alone is not a unique/optimal strategy.",
    "Both independent successful native responses establish feasibility within their own geometry, not that the old response stops being useful after the swap.",
    "A changed first warning/source label, initial distance or primary aim direction alone does not establish a new landing/route/target decision."
  ],
  "source_mechanism": [
    "Actual completed left fork swipe lands nominally(-1.08,-12.674590875), while logical selected ID remains common_left. Original housing is(-.9,-14.5), changed housing(+.9,-14.5). Native source roots/profile/timing/roles/floor/controls remain unchanged.",
    "First original response candidate is down-right. Nominal endpoint(.829188309,-14.583779184) is1.731216671from the old housing, inside ordinary opening reach2-SKIN1.99 and outside the old finite lane. It is only.109696159from the changed source and inside changed padded lane.",
    "Scheduler preserves the escape endpoint through activation: zero-return path waits there until active_until+TIME_MARGIN, and any positioning dash starts no earlier than that opening. Therefore this first old endpoint cannot be made safe against the changed lane merely by choosing a later return.",
    "A source-only possible changed alternative is second down-left escape to(-2.989188309,-14.583779184), followed after active by right return to(-.289188309,-14.583779184),1.192135809from the changed housing. This is not a prescribed path or proof; actual context/view/native floor/capsule/LOS may reject or select another response."
  ],
  "actual_receipts_to_compare": [
    {
      "path": "receipts.old-left/current-left.fork_dash and fork_landing",
      "inspect": "Actual full distance/collision_shortened=false, final landing, route/common_left identity, complete same neutral kit/stats, actual native grounded clock/pose. Use observed positions rather than nominal source arithmetic."
    },
    {
      "path": "receipts.old-left/current-left.armed_plan.state and reservation",
      "inspect": "Actual owner-bound first cycle/lease, source_position, direction, finite lane from/to/radius, profile/role, lock/active/recovery deadlines. Source positions differ only the declared X exchange. Compare phase-relative schedules if fresh run absolute clocks differ; do not assume clocks or native IDs match across instances."
    },
    {
      "path": "receipts.old-left/current-left.armed_plan.proof",
      "inspect": "Actual escape landing, attack_position, path segment kinds/from/to/start/end, ordinary_primary timing and complete cadence. Check whether one old useful path loses active safety or ordinary recovery reach in current committed geometry. Mere different prover selection is insufficient if the same old route remains safe/useful."
    },
    {
      "path": "receipts.old-left/current-left.after_response.actions and phase_receipts",
      "inspect": "Executed world-action dash directions/measured paths/origin/landing/sequence plus ordinary primary direction/hit/gear/stats; warning/lock/active/recovery own-state/lease snapshots and Hero poses/HP. Confirm actual execution corresponds to the retained proof and does not replace it with a forced path or later-cycle retry."
    },
    {
      "path": "receipts.old-left/current-left.after_response.state, final_observation and cleanup",
      "inspect": "Actual selected HP30->10 for neutral, unchanged initial Hero HP, original source/cycle/lease through actual full cadence, empty defeated/checkpoint/progress history, other six living idle actors and normal cleanup. This remains a declared component, not parent save/route authority."
    },
    {
      "path": "receipts.useful_change",
      "inspect": "Current initial-distance boolean row is observational support only. Root semantic review must qualify it against the complete geometry/actions above; do not treat its green status as sufficient novelty credit."
    }
  ],
  "bounded_support_rule": "Within already planned native results, one familiar actually executed old neutral landing/path losing safety or useful ordinary recovery reach against the new committed geometry, together with a different successful current ordinary response, supports this bounded authored landing/approach change. No claim of unique solution, universally invalid old strategies, difficulty increase, measured learning or all-kit balance.",
  "falsifiers_or_insufficient_results": [
    "Native view/context excludes the hypothesized first old escape and both actual runs use the same safe, useful escape/return/ordinary-primary positions. Initial range row may pass while no new movement decision is demonstrated.",
    "Old/current proofs differ only due first-viable ordering or timing noise, but actual old movement path still avoids current active lane and reaches the current opening with original cadence. Different output alone is not novelty.",
    "Either first native cycle refuses, cancels, is incomplete, harms Hero, misses ordinary primary or fails full cadence. Retain actual failure; do not force another path/lease/phase or relax guards.",
    "Actual old path is not this nominal first candidate. Treat that arithmetic prediction as falsified for the run; evaluate actual retained evidence instead. A different demonstrated structural response could still support the candidate, but no extra playthrough/test is required merely to chase this prediction."
  ],
  "review_action": "Keep frozen testcase/wrapper/candidate unchanged during current custody. Root may manually compare the already retained closed native receipts and record an explicit semantic acceptance/qualification. If response options are equivalent, award no authored-policy novelty credit from this component; preserve original accepted A2-L1 and report the limitation.",
